cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use beamrecal, please cite it as below."
title: "beamrecal: geometric recalibration for sensing-aided millimeter-wave beam prediction under deployment shift"
abstract: >-
  Learned sensing-aided beam predictors do not transfer between DeepSense 6G sites, and test-time
  adaptation does not repair them, because the dominant shift rotates and translates the map from sensed
  geometry to beam index. beamrecal implements a physically parameterized position prior and camera map
  that are recalibrated from periodic beam sweeps, a deployable camera pipeline with a pretrained
  detector and position-based identification, the learned and test-time adaptation baselines, and the
  online streaming evaluation that scores every prediction before its feedback arrives.
